// TestTransferFunctionDescriptorChainExactTier: singular-E chain models
// whose float Weierstrass reduction fails closed (infinite Jordan chain left
// among the finite eigenvalues, or a split the pencil solves refute) take
// the exact tier: the exact num/den of the stored data at the convention's
// degrees, verified against the pencil. stiffPoleChainDescriptor seed 2
// (proper [2] beside a stiff pole), refutedChainDescriptor seed 0 (proper
// 3×3, chains beside a large pole) and smallSTermChainDescriptor(14, 1e-4)
// (improper 1×3, s-terms to s^5) were ErrDescriptorSingular from TF,
// IsProper and Step. Oracle: the exact rational response of the stored
// data, within √ε·max(|G|, T) plus the data bound, the contract of the
